# 9. Learning-Quality Rules

| Rule | Classification | Initial Action |
|---|---|---|
| CP-LEARN-001 Real-World Relevance | AI-Assisted + Human | Later |
| CP-LEARN-002 Scenario-First Context | AI-Assisted + Human | Later |
| CP-LEARN-003 Concept Explanation | AI-Assisted + Human | Later |
| CP-LEARN-004 Hands-On Learning | Deterministic structural + AI/Human semantic | Split |
| CP-LEARN-005 Enterprise Equivalent | Deterministic structural + AI/Human semantic | Split |
| CP-LEARN-006 Tangible Output | Deterministic structural + AI/Human semantic | Split |
| CP-LEARN-007 Job Relevance | AI-Assisted + Human | Later |

### Split-rule principle

Some CyberPivot rules contain two different questions.

Example:

> Does the module contain a hands-on section?

This is deterministic.

> Is the hands-on exercise actually useful and appropriate?

This is not deterministic.

The QA system should therefore report them separately rather than pretending one check proves both.

