# 22. Human-Only Responsibilities

Human review remains the final authority for:

1. Technical correctness of important cybersecurity claims
2. Accuracy of real-world incidents
3. Accuracy of enterprise-product behaviour
4. Suitability of recommended tools/resources
5. Quality and safety of hands-on labs
6. Whether a Cabinet artifact is genuinely useful
7. Whether a module feels like real practitioner work
8. Whether the module is publishable
9. Exceptions to standard content rules
10. Final acceptance of AI-generated findings

