# 27. Definition of Done for CP-AUTO-003

CP-AUTO-003 is complete when:

- every CP-AUTO-002 rule has a classification;
- deterministic, AI-assisted, and human responsibilities are separated;
- split rules are explicitly identified;
- the first CLI scope is defined;
- subjective rules are not accidentally converted into hard gates;
- unresolved repository details are documented;
- the classification can be turned directly into implementation and test tickets.

---

# 28. Next Ticket

**CP-AUTO-004 — Define the QA output contract.**

Before writing the validator, define exactly what it returns.

That contract should specify:

- rule ID
- severity
- status
- file
- location
- message
- evidence
- remediation
- validator version
- summary counts
- exit code

This gives Cursor a stable interface to implement against and gives the future GitHub PR gate and AI reviewer the same output format.
